{"aggregate_id": "01M3CM55H5GD129521HZVX663E", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M3CM55HV1DFWW5RARARAB6YR", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-09-25T15:50:14.834520+00:00", "friendly_name": "Implement lane-allocation integrity: fail-closed on destroyed lanes + coord-branch planning-commit hygiene", "mission_id": "01M3CM55H5GD129521HZVX663E", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "implement-lane-recut-and-planning-commit-integrity-01M3CM55", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Two release-blocking reliability defects live in the implement lane-allocation path. When a lane's worktree and branch are both removed while a work package is still in progress, re-running implement silently cuts a new empty lane and reports success, stranding the committed work while status still says in_progress. Separately, on coordination-topology missions the agent claim commit writes the work-package file onto the coordination branch, so the next lane's planning-artifact merge fails with an add/add conflict and the second work package cannot start. This mission makes both paths fail closed / stay correct so the operator is never told the workspace is ready when committed work is unreachable, and every work package on a coord mission can start.", "purpose_tldr": "Stop 'spec-kitty implement' from silently stranding committed work or blocking the second work package on coordination-topology missions.", "target_branch": "fix/implement-lane-recut-and-planning-commit-integrity", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:50:14.843411+00:00"}
